 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No destruction, overturned town or stones drawn: 82-83 are geometric with no plate. A moon for «بقطع من الليل», an hourglass for «إن موعدهم الصبح». 80:7-11 keeps As-Sa'di's «وهذا بحسب الأسباب المحسوسة». 81:14-19 keeps «ولا يلتفت منكم أحد إلا امرأتك» in one chip. Not glossed where the tafsirs differ: «سجيل» (82:10-11) and who «الظالمين» are (83: only Al-Muyassar's general «تهديد لكل عاص»). 82:4-9 is not glossed (first person). STAGING v4: Lut's town by day, as in 11_76-79 (Lut a blue drop labelled Lut, the angels one gold drop labelled the angels). Their sin is never shown or suggested; Lut's family, his daughters and his wife are never drawn. c1 (80-81): his people (three faceless men in dark robes, in the open street at the centre, with no door behind them) are still there while Lut speaks to them (80:1); no gesture inside his wish (80:2-11), and the angels do not appear on the strong support (80:10-11): they appear on 81:1 on the right and speak to Lut (81:2, 81:14, 81:27). The men turn (81:7) and leave the stage on 81:9 (As-Sa'di: they went away threatening Lut with the morning; the blinding is not shown), so they leave on a word of rescue, not of punishment. A moon plate for a part of the night (81:11-13); nobody turns on 81:14-19 (let none of you look back) and nothing stands for his wife; an hourglass for their appointment is the morning (81:24-29). c2 (82-83): the empty town by day (Al-Muyassar 81: their appointment was the morning; never dawn): no person on stage. The ruin event for the town turned upside down (82:4), stones falling on it from 82:7 (rain of stones); the camera tilts to the sky on 82:9 (stones) and goes wide; a seal plate for marked (83:1-3, safe over your Lord), an hourglass for not far from the wrongdoers (83:5-8). Cover: Lut and the angels by day with the moon plate (Lut is rescued)."
 },
